en:
from a discussion of loading a self-propelled gun:
xxx:...All shells with full charge, but the powder in them is in bags. On the command "Full charge!", the bags stay in place. And on the command "Third charge!" 3 bags are thrown out of the shell. It's done manually, but very quickly. Then the unused powder is burned — a gorgeous sight! But about 40 years ago, they'd hand it in, send it for reweighing and completing new shells. Now they consider it too much trouble, for many reasons.
yyy: We didn't hand it in. The field kitchen boils very fast on charges, which is important for cooking. Especially breakfast at minus forty. It just bangs a little and jumps
